<HelpTab>
    <FluentText>
        Admins and Managers edit a dashboard by selecting it on the <a href="/manage/dashboards">Dashboards</a> list.
        It opens in the designer: the widget list on the left, the dashboard in the middle, and the details of
        whatever you've selected on the right.
    </FluentText>

    <HelpSection Title="Adding widgets">
        <ul>
            <li>Drag a widget from the <strong>Widgets</strong> list onto the dashboard and drop it where you want it.</li>
            <li>Or tap a widget in the list to add it in the first free space.</li>
            <li>Use <strong>Search widgets</strong> to find one by name. Widgets for features your company doesn't have are
                shown greyed out with a lock.</li>
            <li>On a tablet or phone, the list opens from the <strong>Add widget</strong> button.</li>
        </ul>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Moving and resizing">
        <ul>
            <li>Drag a widget to move it. Any widget in the way is pushed down to make room, and the green outline shows
                where it will land. Press <strong>Esc</strong> while dragging to put everything back.</li>
            <li>Drag the handles on a widget's right edge, bottom edge or bottom-right corner to resize it. The dashboard
                is 12 columns wide.</li>
            <li>With a widget selected, the arrow keys move it one space and <strong>Shift</strong> with the arrow keys
                resizes it. <strong>Delete</strong> removes it and <strong>Ctrl+D</strong> duplicates it.</li>
            <li>Select the dashboard's background to see its details, where <strong>Tidy up gaps</strong> moves every
                widget up as far as it will go.</li>
            <li>Dragging works with a mouse, a finger or a pen. On a phone, the dashboard scrolls sideways.</li>
        </ul>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Changing a widget">
        <FluentText>Select a widget to show its details on the right (on a phone, in a panel at the bottom):</FluentText>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Title</strong>: give the widget a name, and turn on <strong>Show the title above the widget</strong>
                to show it on the dashboard.</li>
            <li><strong>Size</strong>: type an exact width and height.</li>
            <li><strong>On phones</strong>: turn off <strong>Show this widget on phones</strong> to leave it out on small screens.</li>
            <li><strong>Settings</strong>: what the widget shows. A Text widget's words are typed here. A widget that still needs
                something choosing, like a kiosk for a scoreboard, says <strong>Needs setup</strong>.</li>
            <li><strong>Duplicate</strong> and <strong>Remove</strong>.</li>
        </ul>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Previewing and saving">
        <ul>
            <li>Select <strong>Preview</strong> to see the dashboard as people will, with working buttons and controls. Select
                <strong>Edit</strong> to go back.</li>
            <li>Select the dashboard's background to change its <strong>Name</strong>, <strong>Description</strong> and
                <strong>Row height</strong>.</li>
            <li>Select <strong>Save</strong> (or press <strong>Ctrl+S</strong>). Nothing changes on anyone's screen until you
                do. Under the dashboard's name it says <strong>Unsaved changes</strong> until you've saved.</li>
            <li>Made a mistake? Use the undo and redo arrows in the toolbar, or <strong>Ctrl+Z</strong> and
                <strong>Ctrl+Shift+Z</strong>. Hover over them to see what they'll undo or redo.</li>
            <li>If you try to leave with unsaved changes, Lanyard asks first.</li>
            <li>If someone else saved the same dashboard while you had it open, Lanyard tells you when you save. You can save
                yours over theirs, or cancel and reload the page to see theirs.</li>
        </ul>
        <HelpNote Intent="MessageBarIntent.Warning">
            <strong>Delete dashboard</strong> is in the <strong>⋯</strong> menu and can't be undone. If the dashboard was
            everyone's home screen, people go back to the standard home page.
        </HelpNote>
    </HelpSection>
</HelpTab>
